Subject: [PATCH] net: skip packets consumed by link-layer output

devif_poll_out checks d_len before devif_out, but ARP and neighbor handling
can consume or drop the packet and clear d_len. In particular, arp_out can
clear it while an address lookup is already pending. Calling the transmit
callback afterwards violates its non-empty-packet contract and asserts in
the netdev upper half. The same path may also have transferred the IOB.

Recheck the packet length before loopback, fragmentation or driver dispatch.
Return zero so polling can continue; do not free a possibly transferred IOB.
This is protocol/driver independent and requires no application workaround.

diff --git a/net/devif/devif_poll.c b/net/devif/devif_poll.c
--- a/net/devif/devif_poll.c
+++ b/net/devif/devif_poll.c
@@ -1283,6 +1283,15 @@ int devif_poll_out(FAR struct net_driver_s *dev,
 
   devif_out(dev);
 
+  /* Link-layer handling may have consumed or dropped the packet, for
+   * example while waiting for address resolution.
+   */
+
+  if (dev->d_len == 0)
+    {
+      return 0;
+    }
+
   bstop = devif_loopback(dev);
   if (bstop)
     {
